  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 105 AM CDT Wed Oct 14 2026\n\nThe upper level trough will continue to move south through the\nregion on Friday with a cooler air mass moving over the area.\nHighs on Friday will be in the upper 50s to lower 60s with highs\nin the 60s this weekend. Gusty northerly winds will accompany\nthe cooler air mass on Friday, as gusts up to 35 mph at times\nThursday night into Friday. Winds will gradually decrease Friday\nafternoon/evening as the trough moves off the southeast. \n\nLows Friday night in Saturday morning are expected to drop into\nthe middle to upper 30s. Lows Saturday night into Sunday morning\nwill range from the middle 30s across the eastern Ozarks to the\nlower 40s across southeastern Kansas. Some patchy front could \nbe possible both mornings in valleys and protected areas. \n\nThe ensemble model members show an upper level shortwave trough\nmoving through the region Sunday night into Monday. A drier air\nmass will be in place so mainly just an increase in clouds will\noccur with the disturbance but a few sprinkles/light rain could\noccur but low chance (less then 15%). \n\nA warming trend will occur early to middle of next week as highs\nwarm into the 70s on Monday with highs in the lower 80s \nreturning by mid week.",
